UTDeck (stage 5.1): the overlay's vertex and index buffers stay mapped.

MangoHud mapped both buffers, copied the overlay's vertices into them and unmapped them again on
every frame. Turnip unmaps for real (munmap), so each frame paid for two mmaps, two munmaps and a
page fault on every page the copy touched. Measured with a timing build in PvZ on the Nothing Phone
(1), recording the overlay's drawing took about 0.3-0.4 ms a frame, more than the panel itself at the
frame-rate-only level. The buffers are now mapped once, when they are made, and stay mapped until
their memory is freed (which unmaps it; Vulkan allows freeing mapped memory). The flush before the
GPU reads them stays (the memory is cached and not coherent).

